package com.clenova.app;

/** Offline policy for the current preview only; review before public release. */
final class PrivacyPolicy {
    static final String VERSION="1.7";
    static final String REVISION_DATE="2026-11-27";
    static final String[][] SECTIONS={
        {"Information we store","Clenova stores local preferences, agent and notification settings, selected protection exclusions and activity records. Exclusions may contain file or folder identifiers, names, locations, type and size when available. History can include names, timestamps and sample cleanup metrics. Only one temporary Agent conversation is stored locally, with up to 48 messages. It expires after 24 hours without new messages or replies; expired data is cleared while the app is running or next time it opens. New conversation or app data reset clears it. Previous archived chats are discarded. Activity history is separate. No account is required."},
        {"How information is used","Settings are used to remember your choices, show your local activity and display sample cleanup recommendations. Protection selections are saved for future cleanup functionality. Smart Scan reads accessible media locally on request. It does not run background scans. On Android 11 or later, selected duplicate copies, manually reviewed similar photos, selected large videos and manually selected screenshots can be moved to the system trash only after you review and approve the Android request. Media is moved to system trash, not permanently deleted by Clenova. Swipe Photos reads only accessible photos locally on request, keeps manual choices in memory for the foreground review, and can move explicitly selected and freshly revalidated photos to Android Trash on Android 11 or later after Android approval. No photos or selections are uploaded by this tool. Video Compressor processes chosen videos locally, stores a temporary encoded copy in app cache and saves a separate video only on request. Saved-copy events are included in local activity history. The original can be moved to Android Trash only after the saved copy is reviewed and verified, protection checks pass and Android confirms the request. Photo Compressor locally re-encodes 1 to 100 explicitly selected photos, retains temporary copies in app cache and saves separate verified copies only on request. Re-encoding can change quality and remove metadata. Successful saves are recorded in local history; originals may be moved to Android Trash only after separately selected, verified smaller copies and fresh source and protection checks, followed by Android approval. No automatic upload or removal. Contacts Cleaner reads permitted contacts locally to detect matching names, numbers and incomplete entries. Native linking retains individual account records. Only explicitly confirmed eligible local phone records may be permanently removed; synced or read-only contacts are not directly deleted. You can edit contacts using Android Contacts and export provider-generated vCards to a destination you choose. Contact history stores counts, not names or phone numbers. No contact data is automatically uploaded. App Manager reads launcher-visible apps in the current Android profile, including package metadata and reported permission grants. Optional Usage Access enables available storage and observed usage information; results are kept in memory during review. Android settings handle app storage and permissions. Only explicitly approved eligible apps can be sent to native Android uninstall confirmation. Verified uninstall history stores the app name, count and time locally, not a claimed amount of recovered storage. No app inventory or usage information is automatically uploaded. Speaker Cleaner generates short audio tones locally and checks the device audio route and media volume during an explicitly started foreground session. It does not record microphone audio, change system volume, or detect physical water or damage. No audio data is uploaded. Downloads lists only files explicitly chosen using Android's document picker. Large files lists user-chosen files and scans selected accessible folders locally; folder-scan results are read-only. Unnecessary files uses filename and MIME hints to review user-selected temporary-looking files, incomplete downloads, APK packages and logs. It does not access other apps' private caches. Incomplete downloads and logs are read-only; only old, individually selected and eligible temporary files or APKs in verified Downloads locations can be removed after explicit confirmation. Eligible explicitly selected local Downloads or Documents files may be permanently removed only after separate confirmation and a fresh protection and metadata check; other documents are read-only. Temporary picker access is not persisted."},
        {"Device permissions","The current app requests notification access and, when you start Smart Scan, optional photo and video access; Swipe Photos requests photo access only; Video Compressor requests video access only, or accepts a video selected through the Android document picker. Photo Compressor requests photo access only or accepts individually selected photos through the document picker. Contacts Cleaner requests read access for scanning, and separate write access before approved linking or removal. Android's file and folder picker lets you select specific exclusions; it does not give Clenova unrestricted storage access. Unused apps and App Manager optionally use Android Usage Access to read available usage history, launcher-visible app information and storage statistics on request. These results remain in memory for the current review; no app usage is uploaded or monitored in the background. You can manage or revoke system permissions in Android settings."},
        {"Storage, security and retention","App records are saved in private Android app storage. Automatic app backup is disabled in the current manifest. Other records remain until you clear them, reset the relevant app data or uninstall the app. The temporary conversation follows the expiry rule above. Clenova does not maintain a server-side chat archive. Clenova has no automatic upload, advertising or analytics integration in this preview. Optional private AI relay is off by default; when explicitly connected, the current typed request and up to three previous typed messages in the current conversation are sent to the configured HTTPS relay and Groq. No file lists, scan results or full conversation history are automatically sent. The relay token is memory-only. Groq processing and retention terms apply. Device security also depends on your Android settings."},
        {"Your choices and data controls","Settings > Privacy & data lets you view local data size, export activity history as JSON, clear history or reset local preferences, exclusions and history. Reset does not delete your personal files, revoke Android permissions or remove exported copies. You control where exports are saved."},
        {"External services and sharing","If you choose to send support or feedback email, your email app handles the draft and delivery. Support drafts include app and Android versions; feedback lets you opt out of those details. Your message is received only if you send it. Google Play, email apps and chosen document providers operate under their own privacy terms. A chosen export provider may store a copy in the cloud."},
        {"Changes to this policy","This policy describes the current preview build. We will update the policy before introducing new data practices or publishing the production app. Check the version and revision date shown above."},
        {"Contact us","For privacy questions or requests about information you have sent to us, contact the configured Clenova support email below. Do not send sensitive files or passwords."}
    };
    private PrivacyPolicy(){}
}
